<title>UK: Briton has transatlantic jumbo to himself.</title>
<headline>Briton has transatlantic jumbo to himself.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A British stockbroker returning to London on Sunday from an Easter shopping trip to New York found himself bumped up to first class with 17 flight attendants at his beck and call because he was the only passenger on board.</p>
<p>The British Airways 747 plane was delayed by an electrical fault and all the passengers except Stuart Pike switched to another flight.</p>
<p>&quot;I wasn't in any hurry and didn't mind hanging around so I thought I'd wait. I thought there would be more space on this flight...but I didn't realise just how much,&quot; Pike said.</p>
</text>
